# TTP-2026-0120 — Phantom Taurus NET-STAR Cross-Plane Stitch — IIS Backdoor + Ntospy Credential Interception + SQL sa CSV Exfil Into One Incident
# XQL paste-buffer generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## BIOC — MP-011 w3wp IIS Worker In-Memory Backdoor Child Process
# severity: high
# The IIS worker process w3wp.exe parents a command interpreter or WMI — the observable signature of the NET-STAR IIServerCore in-memory backdoor executing operator commands and AssemblyExecuter loading assemblies in memory. A healthy w3wp.exe serves requests; it does not spawn cmd/powershell/wmic. Compiler children (csc.exe/cvtres.exe) are deliberately excluded because classic ASP.NET/IIS hosts spawn them for legitimate runtime .aspx page compilation, so they are not a reliable anomaly.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter actor_process_image_name = "w3wp.exe"
| filter action_process_image_name in ("cmd.exe", "powershell.exe", "pwsh.exe", "wmic.exe")
| comp count() as backdoor_children by agent_hostname, actor_process_image_name
| filter backdoor_children >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, actor_process_image_name, backdoor_children

## BIOC — MP-011 Ntospy Network Provider DLL Credential Interception
# severity: high
# Ntospy installs a malicious network-provider DLL by writing under HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\NetworkProvider, intercepting plaintext credentials at the authentication-provider layer as users and services log on. Ntospy's NPPSpy-style network-provider registration is documented in Unit 42's Operation Diplomatic Specter report; the NetworkProvider/ProviderOrder registration mechanism is defined by MITRE T1556.008. Legitimate network providers are rare and installed by trusted installers, not by web-server or scripting processes.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.REGISTRY
| filter action_registry_key_name contains "CurrentControlSet\\Control\\NetworkProvider"
| filter action_registry_value_name = "ProviderOrder" or action_registry_data contains ".dll"
| comp count() as provider_writes by agent_hostname, actor_process_image_name
| filter provider_writes >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, actor_process_image_name, provider_writes

## BIOC — MP-011 WMI-Spawned SQL sa CSV Export via mssq bat
# severity: high
# mssq.bat is deployed via WMI Win32_Process.Create and runs sqlcmd against SQL Server using the 'sa' system-administrator login, filtering rows on diplomatic/geographic keywords and exporting matches to CSV. Detect WmiPrvSE.exe parenting cmd/sqlcmd with an 'sa' login and file output — the NET-STAR database-direct exfil stage.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter actor_process_image_name = "WmiPrvSE.exe"
| filter action_process_image_name in ("cmd.exe", "sqlcmd.exe")
| filter action_process_command_line contains "mssq" or action_process_command_line contains "-U sa" or action_process_command_line contains ".csv"
| comp count() as sql_exports by agent_hostname, actor_process_image_name
| filter sql_exports >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, actor_process_image_name, sql_exports

## BIOC — MP-011 IIS Webroot ASPX Timestomp via changeLastModified
# severity: medium
# The IIServerCore changeLastModified command timestomps the OutlookEN.aspx web-shell loader to match a legitimate ASPX file, hiding the implant from modified-time triage. Detect a file-time modification on a .aspx file under the IIS webroot performed by the w3wp.exe worker process itself.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.FILE and event_sub_type = ENUM.FILE_TIMES_MODIFIED
| filter actor_process_image_name = "w3wp.exe"
| filter action_file_path contains "inetpub" and action_file_extension = "aspx"
| filter action_file_modification_time < action_file_creation_time or action_file_modification_time > current_time()
| comp count() as timestomp_events by agent_hostname, action_file_path
| filter timestomp_events >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, action_file_path, timestomp_events

## VALIDATION — MP-011 Anomalous w3wp Child Process Surfaced on IIS Host
# purpose: validation
# dataset: xdr_data

dataset = xdr_data
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 900)
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter actor_process_image_name = "w3wp.exe"
| filter action_process_image_name in ("cmd.exe", "powershell.exe", "pwsh.exe", "wmic.exe")
| comp count() as child_procs by agent_hostname
| filter child_procs >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, child_procs

## VALIDATION — MP-011 STAR-Delimited Encrypted HTTPS Exfil from w3wp
# purpose: hunt
# dataset: xdr_data

dataset = xdr_data
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 900)
| filter event_type = ENUM.NETWORK
| filter actor_process_image_name = "w3wp.exe"
| filter action_remote_port = 443
| comp count() as egress_sessions, sum(action_total_upload) as bytes_out by agent_hostname, action_remote_ip
| filter egress_sessions >= 1
| sort desc bytes_out
| fields agent_hostname, action_remote_ip, egress_sessions, bytes_out

